  entryReasons:
    earlyDaysReasons:
    - Returning to fix the walk-in freezer.
    - Resident returning to home address.
    - Coming back to sharpen the cleavers.
    midDaysReasons:
    - Checking the seals on the back door.
    - Escaping the smog for the night.
    - Picking up more gauze from the clinic.
    finalDaysReasons:
    - Reentering to hide in the basement; the wind is too loud.
    - Returning from the boundary fence; I just wanted to see the sky.
    - Reentering the gates to find a place to sleep that isn't grey.
  invalidEntryReasons:
    earlyDaysReasons:
    - Returning from the 1800s to see the horses.
    - Reentering from the moon; it was very dusty there.
    - Coming back from the clouds to visit a friend.
    midDaysReasons:
    - Returning from the bottom of the ocean; I am dry.
    - Reentering from yesterday; I think I left my keys there.
    - Coming from the center of a volcano to stay warm.
    finalDaysReasons:
    - I am a government inspector here to ensure all radiation safety protocols are
      being met.
    - Coming from a wedding. I was the flower boy.
    - I am here for a routine dental checkup; my gums are just a bit ticklish.
  entryDialogues:
    lastVerdict: 0
    dialoguesEarlyDays:
    - Careful with the permit. My hands are always a bit... slick.
    - The bandages? Just a little accident at the shop. Don't stare.
    - I have a special cut of rib waiting for me inside.
    dialoguesMidDays:
    - The hunger... it isn't in my stomach anymore. It's in my teeth.
    - Do you hear the metal grinding, officer? It never truly stops.
    - I feel the air touching my raw face through the gauze.
    dialoguesFinalDays:
    - Here, take my papers. Sorry got a little blood on them. Comes with the profession.
    - You look like you'd make a good filet mignon.
    - Hope you're not sick of seeing me. Cause I've been dying to see you.
