  introDialogue: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 84cf4fdd911f2254099f3740d809c986, type: 2}
  questionResponses:
  - question: Where are you coming from?
    earlyDaysAnswer: The market. Closing the stall for the evening.
    midDaysAnswer: The back district. Picking up supplies where I can find them.
    finalDaysAnswer: Nowhere worth mentioning.
    mismatchEarlyDaysAnswer: Home. Haven't been out in days. The smell of the street
      has changed. I don't like it anymore.
    mismatchMidDaysAnswer: The market. Fresh as ever. Same faces. Same cuts. Nothing
      unusual at all.
    mismatchFinalDaysAnswer: The shop. Long shift. Everything is running very smoothly.
      Nice and clean.
    uncannyEarlyDaysAnswer: 
    uncannyMidDaysAnswer: 
    uncannyFinalDaysAnswer: 
  - question: Have you been experiencing any strange symptoms lately?
    earlyDaysAnswer: Nothing unusual. My back hurts but it always hurts.
    midDaysAnswer: I've been sweating more than normal. And my vision goes dark sometimes
      when I stand up fast.
    finalDaysAnswer: My hands shake now. Started about a week ago. I can still work.
    mismatchEarlyDaysAnswer: Ha. Symptoms. That's a funny word for it. My back's
      been perfect. Never better. Almost suspiciously better.
    mismatchMidDaysAnswer: Nothing at all. No sweating. Vision's sharp. Honestly,
      I feel... hungry. Very, very hungry.
    mismatchFinalDaysAnswer: My hands are perfectly still. See? Perfectly still.
      I've always had very steady hands.
    uncannyEarlyDaysAnswer: 
    uncannyMidDaysAnswer: 
    uncannyFinalDaysAnswer: 
  - question: Who do you live with?
    earlyDaysAnswer: My brother and his family. Small place, but we manage.
    midDaysAnswer: My brother. His wife left with the kids when the quarantine started.
    finalDaysAnswer: My brother. He doesn't talk much anymore.
    mismatchEarlyDaysAnswer: Just me. Always just me. More room that way. More quiet.
      I enjoy the quiet.
    mismatchMidDaysAnswer: My brother and his whole family. Wife, the kids, very
      full house. Very noisy. I don't mind noise.
    mismatchFinalDaysAnswer: No one. Been alone for years. My brother? No, no. I
      don't have a brother.
    uncannyEarlyDaysAnswer: 
    uncannyMidDaysAnswer: 
    uncannyFinalDaysAnswer: 
  idleBarks:
    earlyDays:
    - Careful with the permit. My hands are always a bit slick.
    - You ever notice how much quieter the streets have gotten at night? I love that.
    - I have a special cut waiting back at the shop. Been looking forward to it all
      day.
    midDays:
    - Do you hear the grinding? It does not stop. I have stopped trying to make it
      stop.
    - People bring me all sorts of things to barter now. I accept most of it. Protein
      is protein.
    - The hunger has gotten very specific lately. Hard to explain over a booth.
    finalDays:
    - You look like you have not slept, officer. Neither have I. I do not miss it.
    - The bandages are dry today. First time in a while. I have been testing a theory.
    - I am having a very productive week. All things considered.
    uncannyEarlyDays: []
    uncannyMidDays: []
    uncannyFinalDays: []
  IDNumber: 9722713
